  📗
    Names an origin of the app itself: what a browser has in its address bar
    for the app's own pages, as in https://shop.example.com. A request from
    there is not a request from another origin, and the policy leaves it
    alone. An app need not say this. A browser of the last years says of
    every request whether it is the site's own (Sec-Fetch-Site), and for the
    others the policy compares the request's Origin with its Host. But
    behind a proxy that writes a Host of its own, that comparison goes by a
    name the proxy chose, and an app that says here what its origin is does
    not depend on it: once one is named, the Host is not looked at. Anything
    that is not an origin is a startup problem.
