    Whether *text* is an origin: a scheme, ://, and a host with or without a
    port, and nothing after it, as in https://app.example.com. What a host
    may hold is letters, digits, dots, hyphens and underscores, a colon
    before the port, and the brackets of an IPv6 address. For an application
    that takes an origin from a setting and wants to know that it is one
    before it puts it anywhere. The word null, which a policy may allow, is
    not an origin here.
